 Every row of the Issues table is reachable with the pointer, at the place the
 pane's WINDOW put it.

 `desk-style-click` is the model. What a miss costs here is quieter than the
 launcher's wrong application and louder than nothing: the reader clicks an
 issue and a DIFFERENT issue is selected, the table repaints with a row
 highlighted, and it looks exactly like a click that worked. `desk-trk-hit`
 had no test of any kind before the pane became a window, and neither did
 anything else in this pane.

 The sweep hoists the layout out of the probe for the reason `desk-calc-click`
 gives, and the spot checks go through `desk-trk-hit` itself so the shipped
 function is not left untested.

 THE PLACED ROW IS WHAT MAKES THE OTHERS MEAN ANYTHING. `desk-trk-hit` reads
 the pane's block out of `dk-trk-cell` to find the window rect; an unwritten
 cell reads zero, address zero reads back as zeros, and zeros are
 `dk-wnd-st-normal` with a width of zero -- the never-placed sentinel -- so the
 WRONG block yields exactly the default rect the right block yields. Every row
 above agrees under both. The last row places a window on its own block, at a
 rect the default arithmetic cannot produce.

 The table is asked for the row rather than for a widget id, because the id
 carries the ABSOLUTE index across the whole filtered list and that is what a
 selection is. The state is built once and shared: `gtk-row-at` rebuilds the
 table on every call, which a twelve thousand point sweep cannot afford.

 TWO SABOTAGES, RUN SEPARATELY, AND THE SWEEP SEES NEITHER. Laying
 `desk-trk-hit`'s tree back at the screen corner under the chrome moves the
 placed row from 23 of 23 to 10, and reading its block from address zero
 instead of `dk-trk-cell` moves it to 10 as well. `reachable` reads
 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 under both, because it never calls `desk-trk-hit` at all: it
 asks which rows the reference layout exposes, which is a question about the
 table and not about where the window put it.

Section: Test

  tc-at : WidgetNode, DataTableState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tc-at (laid) (dt) (x) (y) =
    when ev-hit-widget laid x y
      is Just (wgt) -> data-table-row-of-hit dt (wgt.wn-id)
      is None -> 0 - 1

  tc-row : WidgetNode, DataTableState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tc-row (laid) (dt) (seen) (x) (y) =
    if x >= 1024 then 0
    else let r = tc-at laid dt x y
    in let p = if r >= 0 & r < 64 then poke-byte seen r 1 else 0
    in tc-row laid dt seen (x + 8) y

  tc-grid : WidgetNode, DataTableState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tc-grid (laid) (dt) (seen) (y) =
    if y >= 768 then 0
    else let r = tc-row laid dt seen 0 y
    in tc-grid laid dt seen (y + 8)

  tc-seen : Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  tc-seen (seen) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 64 then acc
    else if peek-byte seen i == 1 then tc-seen seen (i + 1) (acc & " " & integer-to-text i)
    else tc-seen seen (i + 1) acc

  tc-yn : Boolean -> Text
  tc-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

 A CENSUS DOWN THE COLUMN, NOT ONE POINT. The first version of this asked the
 two layouts to agree at the FIRST point the reference answered a row, and
 that point is where the corner layout has its own first row: both said row
 zero and the sabotage moved nothing at all. One sample cannot separate two
 layouts that necessarily agree somewhere. Every eighth pixel down a column
 inside the window can, because the row a y lands on differs between them
 everywhere except at the crossing.

 The count is `points * 1000 + agreements`, one integer because that is what a
 recursion can carry back, and both halves are printed so a drop in either is
 visible.

  tc-census : WidgetNode, DataTableState, DbServer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tc-census (laid) (dt) (srv) (ds) (x) (y) =
    if y >= 768 then 0
    else let r = tc-at laid dt x y
    in let a = if r < 0 then 0
      else if desk-trk-hit 1024 768 x y ds srv 0 0 gfont-none == r then 1001
      else 1000
    in a + tc-census laid dt srv ds x (y + 8)

 The window's content box in LOGICAL units, which is what `comp-render-at`
 lays a window's tree out in and therefore what `desk-trk-hit` divides into.
 The table height comes from the shipped measuring pass, because the tree the
 paint drew and the tree a click is resolved against must be the same one; the
 RECT is duplicated here, because that is the thing under test.

  tc-tree : Integer, Integer, Integer, DbServer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  tc-tree (w) (h) (ds) (srv) (filter) (sel) =
    let box = desk-trk-win-box w h srv filter sel ds gfont-none
    in let s = ui-wscale w
    in let blk = peek-32 ds dk-trk-cell
    in let st = dk-wnd-st blk
    in let bh = dk-wnd-bar-h gfont-none s
    in let wx = dk-wnd-rx blk w st ds
    in let wy = dk-wnd-ry blk w h st ds + bh
    in let ww = dk-wnd-rw blk w st ds
    in let wh = dk-wnd-rh blk w h st ds - bh
    in widget-layout (gtk-tree srv filter sel (box.lr-h) (box.lr-w)) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect (wx / s) (wy / s) (ww / s) (wh / s))

  tc-state : Integer, Integer, Integer, DbServer, Integer, Integer -> DataTableState
  tc-state (w) (h) (ds) (srv) (filter) (sel) =
    let box = desk-trk-win-box w h srv filter sel ds gfont-none
    in gtk-data-table srv filter sel (box.lr-h) (box.lr-w)

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let seen = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let gp = poke-32 ds desk-gpu-cell 1
    in let tp = poke-32 ds dk-trk-cell (alloc-zeroed 64 64)
    in let srv = tk-init-tracker-db
    in let laid = tc-tree 1024 768 ds srv 0 0
    in let dt = tc-state 1024 768 ds srv 0 0
    in let g = tc-grid laid dt seen 0
    in let ds2 = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap2 = poke-32 ds2 dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let gp2 = poke-32 ds2 desk-gpu-cell 1
    in let tp2 = poke-32 ds2 dk-trk-cell (alloc-zeroed 64 64)
    in let blk2 = peek-32 ds2 dk-trk-cell
    in let pl = dk-wnd-place blk2 (dk-wnd-x 1024 dk-wnd-st-normal ds2 + 40) (dk-wnd-y 1024 768 dk-wnd-st-normal ds2 + 24) 600 400
    in let pl-tree = tc-tree 1024 768 ds2 srv 0 0
    in let pl-dt = tc-state 1024 768 ds2 srv 0 0
    in let pl-x = dk-wnd-x 1024 dk-wnd-st-normal ds2 + 40 + 100
    in let pl-c = tc-census pl-tree pl-dt srv ds2 pl-x 0
    in let pl-rows = pl-c / 1000
    in let pl-agree = int-mod pl-c 1000
    in act
      print-line-uni ("reachable" & tc-seen seen 0 "")
      print-line-uni ("miss row=" & integer-to-text (desk-trk-hit 1024 768 0 0 ds srv 0 0 gfont-none))
      print-line-uni ("sidebar row=" & integer-to-text (desk-trk-hit 1024 768 60 300 ds srv 0 0 gfont-none))
      print-line-uni ("placed: " & integer-to-text pl-rows & " row points, " & integer-to-text pl-agree & " agree, all " & tc-yn (pl-rows > 0 & pl-rows == pl-agree))
      print-line-uni ("title " & desk-wnd-title desk-focus-trk & "  block " & tc-yn (desk-wnd-blk desk-focus-trk ds == peek-32 ds dk-trk-cell))
    end

